  "caption": "Quinn joined a CrossFit box, chased the clock on rep 47, and woke up with shoulders on strike.\n\nFatigue is often where things go wrong: as a set wears on, technique can slip, the back may round and the shoulders start doing extra work.\n\nWhat often helps: end the set when your form breaks, not when the timer says so; scale consistently; build strict strength before kipping; and warm up for the positions the workout asks for, easing in over your first months. Don't train through a familiar ache.\n\nIf pain is there before you start, or keeps showing up in one spot, get it checked. Severe muscle pain out of proportion to a session or dark urine needs a same-day medical review.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
